# Build-Depends is the one list the release's Ubuntu legs install
# (`apt-get build-dep ./packaging/deb`), as the spec's BuildRequires is
# for Fedora. debhelper compat 13: Ubuntu 26.04 ships debhelper 13.31,
# so 13 is the highest level both supported releases build. The rustc
# floor is Cargo.toml's rust-version (tests/deb-package.sh holds it).
#
# Depends is computed: ${shlibs:Depends} names what the binaries link
# (libc6 and libgcc-s1; wayland-backend's pure-Rust backend never loads
# libwayland), and the supervisor calls systemctl (systemd) and
# dbus-update-activation-environment (dbus-bin) on every login. river
# and zellij are deliberately absent: no Ubuntu archive carries either,
# and the README's PPA and zellij steps cover them (ADR-013). The
# Recommends are what the default config drives, the two portal
# backends buoy-portals.conf names, and notify-send, which buoy-wm
# spawns when it rejects a config.
Source: buoy-wm
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Nick Booth <nick@onlyhams.radio>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cargo,
               rustc (>= 1.93),
               libwayland-dev,
               pkgconf
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/nkbooth/buoy-wm
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: buoy-wm
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, dbus-bin, systemd
Recommends: foot,
            fuzzel,
            xdg-desktop-portal-wlr,
            xdg-desktop-portal-gtk,
            libnotify-bin
Suggests: waybar
Description: keyboard-driven window manager for the river Wayland compositor
 buoy manages windows for the river Wayland compositor (0.4+) via
 river-window-management-v1. It owns all tag state itself and gives each
 tag a persistent fullscreen terminal multiplexer pinned behind every
 other window, with graphical applications floating above it. Every
 operation is bound to the keyboard and every binding is rebindable
 through one TOML file.
 .
 Ships three binaries: the window manager, a fuzzel-driven tag picker,
 and a waybar status-bar feeder.
 .
 Also installs a buoy session for the display manager: river starts a
 supervisor that imports the session into systemd and D-Bus, keeps
 buoy-session.target up exactly as long as the window manager runs, and
 routes screen capture through the wlroots portal backend.
